   "body": "<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\n<!-- review_stack_entry_start -->\n\n<a href=\"https://app.coderabbit.ai/change-stack/ezzz/HFRnow/pull/688?scope=ghh_OusAJGA4HG8ljoOV0wJvVx8NmnZIjc2DdjmxOu0xZWA&amp;cs_source=review_comment\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-stack-buttons-v1/explain-change-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-stack-buttons-v1/explain-change.svg\"><img src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-stack-buttons-v1/explain-change.svg\" alt=\"Explain Change →\" height=\"32\"></picture></a>\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_end -->\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Walkthrough</strong></summary>\n<dl>\n<dd>\n<br>\n\nThe changelog adds an entry for PR `#640`. The migration gap report adds GAP-209 and updates its UX, total, and classification counts.\n\n**Changes: Blacklist and whitelist ledger**\n\n|Layer / File(s)|Summary|\n|:---|:---|\n|**Record PR `#640` and GAP-209** <br> `docs/CHANGELOG-LEGACY.md`, `docs/migration/GAP-LEGACY-VS-SWIFT.md`|The changelog describes blacklist and whitelist settings and commands. The gap report documents the profile-sheet behavior after a pseudo-list toggle and updates its counts and classification. |\n\n<!-- change_assessment_start -->\n**Estimated code review effort:** 1 (Trivial) | ~5 minutes\n\n<!-- change_assessment_commit:\"ca840d3eae2b9284e35560c569630821d5b152b1\" -->\n<!-- change_assessment_priority:{\"version\":1,\"urgency\":\"p3\",\"manual\":false} -->\n**Change:** Other\n<!-- change_assessment_end -->\n\n**Possibly related issues**\n- [ezzz/HFRnow#687](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/issues/687) — The issue concerns follow-up wording for the same ledger entries.\n- [ezzz/HFRnow#209](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/issues/209) — This issue tracks LOT-118, which the changelog and gap report record.\n\n**Possibly related PRs**\n- [ezzz/HFRnow#674](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/pull/674) — This PR edits the same ledger files and generated counts, which may need reconciliation.\n- [ezzz/HFRnow#650](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/pull/650) — This PR updates the same ledger files and generated totals and classification counts.\n\n**Suggested labels:** `direct-pr`, `ledger`\n\n**Suggested reviewers:** `ezzz`\n\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Merge Risk:</strong> <strong><picture><img src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/risk-unassessed-16.svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\"></picture> Minimal</strong> · up to <code>ca840</code></summary>\n<dl>\n<dd>\n<br>\n\n<!-- final_review_risk_start -->\n<!-- final_review_risk_label\n**Merge Risk:** **⚪ Minimal** · up to `ca840`\n-->\n<!-- final_review_risk_coverage:{\"sourceCommitId\":\"ca840d3eae2b9284e35560c569630821d5b152b1\",\"coveredCommitId\":\"ca840d3eae2b9284e35560c569630821d5b152b1\",\"kind\":\"reviewed\"} -->\n\nThe ledger records the profile-list change without modifying application behavior. No merge-blocking risk is established; the lot-classification follow-up remains unverified.\n<!-- final_review_risk_end -->\n\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Architecture risk:</strong> <strong><picture><img src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/risk-low-16.svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\"></picture> Low</strong> · up to <code>ca840</code></summary>\n<dl>\n<dd>\n<br>\n\n<!-- architecture_review_start -->\n<!-- architecture_review_label\n### Architecture Summary\n\n**Architecture risk:** **🔵 Low** · up to `ca840`\n-->\n\nThe change affects 1 system.\n\n**Changed systems:** `docs`\n\n**Architecture concerns**\nNo architecture-level concerns identified.\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Review details</strong></summary>\n<dl>\n<dd>\n<br>\n\n**Systems and components**\n- _observed_ — docs (service) was modified; 2 changed files map to changed impact.\n\n**Before / after behavior**\n- _observed_ — Modified behavior in docs/CHANGELOG-LEGACY.md: Ajout de l’entrée `#640`, qui décrit les options de modification des listes noire et blanche et les commandes de blacklist/whitelist dans les réglages, le menu du membre et le profil.\n- _observed_ — Modified behavior in docs/migration/GAP-LEGACY-VS-SWIFT.md: The report adds GAP-209, documenting that the profile sheet stays open and displays a sentence after a pseudo-list toggle; closing the sheet rebuilds the reader without making a request.\n- _observed_ — Modified behavior in docs/migration/GAP-LEGACY-VS-SWIFT.md: The generated Counts table raises UX-change rows from 46 to 47 and total rows from 167 to 168; other listed gap counts remain unchanged.\n- _observed_ — Modified behavior in docs/migration/GAP-LEGACY-VS-SWIFT.md: The H.1 classification heading increases the classified-row count from 122 to 123. GAP-209 is added to class `b`, raising its count from 48 to 49; the other class assignments and counts remain unchanged.\n\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</details>\n<!-- architecture_review_end -->\n\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</details>\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Pre-merge checks: <sup><picture><img src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/pre-merge-checks-counter-passed-14-v2.svg\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" align=\"middle\" alt=\"Passed\" title=\"Passed\"></picture></sup> 4 · <sup><picture><img src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/pre-merge-checks-counter-inconclusive-14-v2.svg\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" align=\"middle\" alt=\"Inconclusive\" title=\"Inconclusive\"></picture></sup> 1</strong></summary>\n<dl>\n<dd>\n<br>\n\n<strong><sup><picture><img src=\"https: